lds remain unresolved; no epsilon, tick/pip/point tolerance, minimum body size, or percentage threshold is defined. A candidate high remains provisional until a formally closed Close < prior LL confirms the new LL and validates the preceding highest candidate high as LH only from that causal AsOfUtc; wick-only penetration and an open candle do not confirm it. Within one recognized bearish correction, a higher candidate high replaces a lower candidate and superseded intermediate highs do not survive as LH. This confirms LH structural identity and its selected-turn structural coordinate: the highest Open or Close body edge; candle color does not alter it and a higher wick does not redefine it. Structural coordinates remain distinct from the buy HL Low/lowest-wick and sell LH High/highest-wick protection anchors. The causal confirming candle is excluded from the correction set and retrospective candidate HL/LH scan, belongs conceptually to the impulsive leg, and its formally closed Close validates the new HH/LL and preceding candidate only from that causal AsOfUtc. In the single-expansive-candle case, its Open supplies the structural HL/LH origin coordinate and its Close supplies causal validation without making it a correction candle or requiring an intrabar path. This does not replace multi-candle body-edge rules. Opening/quotation gaps have no independent structural role: previous Close != current Open neither starts nor fragments a correction, resets it, invalidates structure, creates or validates HH/HL/LH/LL, nor has a size threshold. Exact body direction governs correction start; strict High > current correction-origin ceiling or Low < current correction-origin floor governs reset; and formally closed Close beyond prior validated HL/LH governs invalidation. An Open beyond a level, including a gap Open across HL/LH without the qualifying Close, is not an independent reset or invalidation event; equality and wick-only penetration remain non-invalidating. No synthetic interpolation, candles, or interbar path is inferred. Opening gaps are distinct from FVG/IFVG and do not resolve their geometry, size, fill, or 1M interaction. No fixed candle/day/session count, historical time window, scan count, or numeric pivot/fractal lookback defines 4H bootstrap. Once valid structural references exist, the latest strict formally closed body break above an upper reference inherits bullish context and the latest strict formally closed body break below a lower reference inherits bearish context; equality and wick-only penetration do not qualify, and future data cannot supply the break. The resulting latest HH plus originating/validated HL or latest LL plus originating/validated LH becomes the operational active pair under the existing causal rules, while older structure remains audit evidence. Post-anchor structural mechanics are substantially causal and deterministic. Exact equal body coordinates within one selected turn form one price-based structural level; no individual candle ownership or first/last/timestamp/sequence tie-break is required, duplicate structural points are not created, and a wick-based ProtectionAnchor may come from another candle in that turn. Remaining deterministic blockers are initial structural anchor selection from arbitrary raw 4H candles and termination/boundary of that initial historical scan, plus near-doji/small-body threshold, remaining candle inclusivity, near-equal structural zone tolerance, and other structural coordinate/boundary edge cases. Viewport, zoom, screen width, arbitrary loaded-history count, weekly open, previous-day extrema, and Asia/London levels are not deterministic anchor selectors or mandatory seeds. When one formally closed candle has both High > current correction-origin ceiling and Close < prior validated HL, both observations coexist but prior-HL invalidation dominates the structural transition. From that causal AsOfUtc, bullish structure is invalidated, the candidate HL is destroyed, and the collision candle starts no new bullish correction: it is excluded from the old bullish turn and candidate geometry and belongs to the new bearish impulse context. Its High remains a relevant upper price extreme and bearish-origin reference with wick-based protection evidence, but is not an automatically validated LH, structural High, or executable Stop Loss; the old StructuralPrice and ProtectionAnchor remain unchanged. Earlier historical evaluations are not reinterpreted. No intrabar chronology, Step-3/Step-4 mapping, IFVG/FVG inference, entry gating, or same-frame propagation is implied.", NasdaqSource),
        Blocked("moneyway-nasdaq", "nasdaq-0.1.0-draft", "NQ-M5-004", "The deterministic IFVG geometry remains unresolved.", NasdaqSource),
        Blocked("moneyway-nasdaq", "nasdaq-0.1.0-draft", "NQ-SL-001", "Deterministic identification of the relevant structural 5M HL/LH and executable Stop Loss price/offset remain unresolved. The confirmed buy protection anchor is the Low/lowest wick extreme of the relevant structural 5M HL; the confirmed sell protection anchor is the High/highest wick/tail of the relevant structural 5M LH. Those anchors remain separate from structural coordinates, including the single-candle origin Open. This does not define an executable Stop Loss price, buffer, tick distance, spread/cost adjustment, broker order, or execution semantics.", NasdaqSource),
