es not start. A formally closed Close < prior validated HL invalidates the bullish structure and ends pursuit of that candidate; the invalidation candle is excluded from the destroyed turn and candidate geometry, cannot alter its StructuralPrice or ProtectionAnchor, and is new bearish impulse evidence rather than a validated structural LL. Close == prior validated HL and wick-only Low < prior validated HL with Close >= prior validated HL do not invalidate. An invalidated bullish structure cannot yield a validated HL usable as a structural fallback target candidate. Until a formally closed Close > prior HH, deeper lows replace shallower candidates, and only that causal close makes the candidate usable from its AsOfUtc. Within a selected turn, the lowest Open or Close body price is source-supported and an isolated wick is insufficient. Direct bearish evidence confirms the correction start for the demonstrated case: the prior LL remains the structural reference and, after the bearish impulse stops producing new lows, the first bullish candle that begins upward displacement starts the correction. When the LL-producing candle is distinct, it remains in the prior bearish impulse and outside the new correction; an exact-doji LL candle before that first bullish body is likewise excluded. Its Open, Close, High, and Low cannot alter the new candidate turn StructuralPrice or ProtectionAnchor. If that same first bullish candle prints a new lower Low, the new lower extreme takes precedence: update the correction-origin floor to that Low, then start the correction only if the same candle closes bullish. That updated floor is a price extreme, not an automatically validated structural LL; LL validation still requires its causal formally closed body below the prior structural LL, and no synthetic intrabar chronology is inferred. The floor and ceiling precedence cases are symmetric without conflating either correction-origin extreme with a validated structural HH/LL. An exact doji with Close == Open is directionally neutral and starts neither correction. If it prints a new higher High or new lower Low, update the applicable correction-origin ceiling or floor but leave correction not started; the update neither turns the doji into an opposite-direction start candle nor validates a structural HH/LL. At that doji AsOfUtc, later candles cannot retroactively create a correction start. Near-doji/small-body thresholds remain unresolved; no epsilon, tick/pip/point tolerance, minimum body size, or percentage threshold is defined. A candidate high remains provisional until a formally closed Close < prior LL confirms the new LL and validates the preceding highest candidate high as LH only from that causal AsOfUtc; wick-only penetration and an open candle do not confirm it. Within one recognized bearish correction, a higher candidate high replaces a lower candidate and superseded intermediate highs do not survive as LH. This confirms candidate-LH identity and its selected-turn target structural coordinate: the highest Open or Close body edge; candle color does not alter it and a higher wick does not redefine it. This body-based target coordinate is distinct from buy/sell protection wick anchors; neither substitutes for the other. The causal confirming candle is excluded from the correction set and retrospective candidate HL/LH scan, belongs conceptually to the impulsive leg, and its formally closed Close validates the new HH/LL and preceding candidate only from that causal AsOfUtc. In the single-expansive-candle case, its Open supplies the structural HL/LH origin coordinate and its Close supplies causal validation without making it a correction candle or requiring an intrabar path. This does not replace multi-candle body-edge rules or use a protection wick as a target coordinate. Opening/quotation gaps have no independent structural fallback role: previous Close != current Open neither starts nor fragments a correction, resets it, invalidates structure, creates or validates HH/HL/LH/LL, nor creates a structural target or has a size threshold. Only causally validated structural points may enter fallback. Exact body direction governs correction start; strict High > current correction-origin ceiling or Low < current correction-origin floor governs reset; and formally closed Close beyond prior validated HL/LH governs invalidation. An Open beyond a level, including a gap Open across HL/LH without the qualifying Close, is not an independent reset or invalidation event; equality and wick-only penetration remain non-invalidating. No synthetic interpolation, candles, or interbar path is inferred. Opening gaps are distinct from FVG/IFVG and do not resolve their geometry, size, fill, or 1M interaction. Once structure is established, structural fallback may use only causally validated 1H/4H points under the documented rules. No fixed candle/day/session count, historical time window, scan count, or numeric pivot/fractal lookback defines H4 bootstrap. The remaining H4 bootstrap boundary is initial structural anchor selection from arbitrary raw candles and termination/boundary of the initial historical scan; session/context levels are not mandatory H4 seeds. Exact equal structural body coordinates within one selected turn collapse to one price-based structural fallback candidate level; no individual candle ownership or first/last/timestamp/sequence tie-break is required, and it may be used only when otherwise causally valid. Remaining structural reconstruction blockers are that boundary, near-doji/small-body threshold, remaining candle inclusivity, near-equal structural zone tolerance, and other structural coordinate/boundary edge cases. Other structural-point selection and coordinate/boundary edge cases, exact OHLC mitigation test, PDH/PDL cross-class ranking, and distinct target-level ties or coincidences remain unresolved. General final Take Profit hierarchy outside the reviewed cases and universal full-exit behavior also remain